1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,442
Welcome to CareConsent.

2
00:00:02,442 --> 00:00:06,835
This app records what each patient agrees
to about the use of their personal

3
00:00:06,835 --> 00:00:08,442
information.

4
00:00:08,442 --> 00:00:12,680
The menu on the left only shows the
screens you need for your job, so you will

5
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:16,216
not see screens meant for the privacy
office.

6
00:00:16,216 --> 00:00:21,311
At the top of every screen there is a box
called Need help with this screen.

7
00:00:21,311 --> 00:00:26,002
Open it to read what the screen is for,
how to fill it in, and answers to common

8
00:00:26,002 --> 00:00:27,490
questions.

9
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:31,920
There is also a button to watch a short
video, like this one.

10
00:00:32,642 --> 00:00:37,687
When you fill in a form, look for the
small round i next to each box.

11
00:00:37,687 --> 00:00:42,603
Move your mouse over it, or tap it on a
tablet, and a short note explains what to

12
00:00:42,603 --> 00:00:45,508
type and why the hospital needs it.

13
00:00:45,508 --> 00:00:50,008
Here, the note explains that the date of
birth tells us whether the patient is a

14
00:00:50,008 --> 00:00:51,294
child.

15
00:00:51,294 --> 00:00:55,391
A child needs a parent or guardian to make
the choices.

16
00:00:56,100 --> 00:01:00,109
The Overview screen is a quick picture of
today's work.

17
00:01:00,109 --> 00:01:04,347
The numbers at the top show how many
patients are registered, how many have

18
00:01:04,347 --> 00:01:08,133
given their choices, and how many are
still waiting.

19
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:12,371
Awaiting consent means nobody has asked
the patient yet.

20
00:01:12,371 --> 00:01:14,883
It does not stop treatment.

21
00:01:14,883 --> 00:01:19,335
Use the Register patient button when
someone new arrives, or click a patient's

22
00:01:19,335 --> 00:01:22,209
name to carry on where you left off.

23
00:01:22,933 --> 00:01:27,266
Before you register anyone, open the
Patient directory and search for the

24
00:01:27,266 --> 00:01:30,228
patient's name or hospital number.

25
00:01:30,228 --> 00:01:33,787
This avoids creating the same patient
twice.

26
00:01:33,787 --> 00:01:38,978
The hospital number is the patient's
record number from the hospital system.

27
00:01:38,978 --> 00:01:41,418
It is not a branch number.

28
00:01:41,418 --> 00:01:45,621
If the patient is already listed, click
their name instead of registering them

29
00:01:45,621 --> 00:01:46,905
again.

30
00:01:47,642 --> 00:01:50,794
Click Register patient and fill in the
form.

31
00:01:50,794 --> 00:01:55,103
Type the full name, the hospital number
and the date of birth.

32
00:01:55,103 --> 00:01:59,794
Choose whose phone it is, then type the
ten digit mobile number.

33
00:01:59,794 --> 00:02:04,472
If the patient wants messages by email,
add their email address and tick the box

34
00:02:04,472 --> 00:02:06,342
to say they agreed.

35
00:02:06,342 --> 00:02:09,151
Never type an Aadhaar number here.

36
00:02:09,151 --> 00:02:12,934
When you are done, click Save and review
choices.

37
00:02:13,642 --> 00:02:16,770
Next you will see the patient's choices.

38
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:21,544
The notice at the top explains, in the
patient's own language, how the hospital

39
00:02:21,544 --> 00:02:23,806
will use their information.

40
00:02:23,806 --> 00:02:28,925
Read it with the patient, or use the
button to have the device read it aloud.

41
00:02:28,925 --> 00:02:32,472
Then let the patient tick each use they
agree to.

42
00:02:32,472 --> 00:02:35,865
Optional uses never affect their
treatment.

43
00:02:35,865 --> 00:02:40,068
Finally, send the one-time code to the
patient's phone and type the code they

44
00:02:40,068 --> 00:02:41,887
read back to you.

45
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:47,100
The Consent register lists every choice
that has been recorded, with the date and

46
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,383
the person who recorded it.

47
00:02:49,383 --> 00:02:54,907
Use it to check what a patient agreed to
before you share or use their information.

48
00:02:54,907 --> 00:02:59,788
If a patient changes their mind, open
their record and choose Withdraw.

49
00:02:59,788 --> 00:03:02,585
Withdrawing stops future use.

50
00:03:02,585 --> 00:03:05,180
It does not cancel their care.

51
00:03:05,892 --> 00:03:07,806
Mistakes happen.

52
00:03:07,806 --> 00:03:13,270
If a phone number, email, date of birth or
notice language was typed wrongly, open

53
00:03:13,270 --> 00:03:16,663
the patient's record from the Patient
directory.

54
00:03:16,663 --> 00:03:20,246
You will see their details and every
choice they made.

55
00:03:20,246 --> 00:03:23,144
Click Edit details to correct them.

56
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:26,752
Change only the box that is wrong.

57
00:03:26,752 --> 00:03:30,550
Leave the mobile number blank if it is
still correct.

58
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:35,002
You can add or change the patient's email,
and change the language their notice is

59
00:03:35,002 --> 00:03:36,454
shown in.

60
00:03:36,454 --> 00:03:41,335
If a new date of birth would make the
patient a child, only a privacy officer

61
00:03:41,335 --> 00:03:42,966
can save it.

62
00:03:42,966 --> 00:03:47,395
Type a short reason for the change, then
click Save changes.

63
00:03:47,395 --> 00:03:50,607
The change is kept in the record's
history.

64
00:03:51,308 --> 00:03:56,496
Patients can ask to see their information,
correct it, or have it removed.

65
00:03:56,496 --> 00:04:01,388
When a patient asks, open Patient rights
and click New request.

66
00:04:01,388 --> 00:04:05,948
Find the patient, choose the type of
request, and write down what they asked

67
00:04:05,948 --> 00:04:08,043
for in their own words.

68
00:04:08,043 --> 00:04:13,460
Check their identity as your hospital
requires, and note how you checked it.

69
00:04:13,460 --> 00:04:16,720
The privacy office will take it from
there.

70
00:04:17,433 --> 00:04:23,811
Before records go to another hospital, a
lab or an insurer, write it down here.

71
00:04:23,811 --> 00:04:27,668
Open Data sharing and click Record sharing
approval.

72
00:04:27,668 --> 00:04:32,442
Find the patient, type the name of the
organisation, and choose why the records

73
00:04:32,442 --> 00:04:34,109
are being shared.

74
00:04:34,109 --> 00:04:38,121
Pick only the smallest set of information
that is needed.

75
00:04:38,121 --> 00:04:41,121
This screen keeps a note of the approval.

76
00:04:41,121 --> 00:04:43,685
It does not send the records.

77
00:04:44,392 --> 00:04:48,342
Doctors and nurses see a slightly
different menu.

78
00:04:48,342 --> 00:04:52,330
You can look up patients and their
choices, and you also have Procedure

79
00:04:52,330 --> 00:04:53,734
records.

80
00:04:53,734 --> 00:04:58,592
You will not see reception tasks such as
sharing approvals, or privacy office

81
00:04:58,592 --> 00:04:59,989
screens.

82
00:05:00,725 --> 00:05:05,213
Procedure records link a patient to the
signed paper or electronic form for a

83
00:05:05,213 --> 00:05:07,984
procedure, such as surgery.

84
00:05:07,984 --> 00:05:12,651
Click Record procedure evidence, choose
the patient, type the procedure name and

85
00:05:12,651 --> 00:05:16,925
the doctor, then type the reference number
of the signed form.

86
00:05:16,925 --> 00:05:21,282
This does not replace the procedure
consent form itself.

87
00:05:21,282 --> 00:05:25,186
The doctor must still explain the
procedure and have the patient sign the

88
00:05:25,186 --> 00:05:26,882
approved form.

89
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:31,707
Readiness and settings shows your account
and how the hospital has set up

90
00:05:31,707 --> 00:05:33,419
CareConsent.

91
00:05:33,419 --> 00:05:38,228
Here you can switch on a sign-in code app
for extra safety, and see the training

92
00:05:38,228 --> 00:05:40,811
your hospital has assigned to you.

93
00:05:40,811 --> 00:05:45,204
You can change the screen language and the
light or dark look from the boxes at the

94
00:05:45,204 --> 00:05:47,372
top of every screen.

95
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:52,061
Patients who have an account see their own
privacy page.

96
00:05:52,061 --> 00:05:56,597
They can check the choices they made,
change or withdraw them, send a request

97
00:05:56,597 --> 00:06:00,419
about their information, and download a
summary.

98
00:06:00,419 --> 00:06:04,728
If a patient asks how to do this, show
them this page.

99
00:06:04,728 --> 00:06:09,371
If they cannot use a phone or computer,
they can always ask at the front desk

100
00:06:09,371 --> 00:06:10,729
instead.
